I want to start working on a gui for this codebase. The goal is to have a gui that runs as a web-application in both the pc and the raspberrypy. The gui will connect to the server using the opc-ua interface and must expose all the read/write variables and methods implemented so far. My suggestion is to use nicegui framework, but suggest other frameworks that could be adequate for this goal. 

Note: determine if psycopg3 can be installed in a raspberry pi 4 and if we can use the same sql module already written in the raspberry. Implement a way to disable the features that depend on it on the server side when its not available. If it can't be installed, suggest other data recording features, but leave it as future work. Implementing a dedicated server side sql interface is out of the scope of these requirements.

