	- An experiment interface that must:
		- let the operator create new experiments
		- let the operator start and assign reactors to an experiment.
		- let the operator start, re-start or stop recording data.
		- let the operator stop the experiment.
		- let the operator export all data associated with the experiment.
		- Suggestion: modify the data table in the sql module to add an experiment_name column and update the necessary logic in client.py from the opcua module
	- Let the user start, resume, stop recording data outside of the experiment interface
	- A live plot interface (scatter plots) for each reactor that must:
		- have a separate plots for ph, dissolved oxygen, temperature and biomass values
		- let the user choose which biomass sensor channels to plot (single or multiple channels)
		- Use datetime format for the x axis instead of mins/hours/days.
		- let the user choose the time frame to plot (ie. plot the last 24h or the last 2h)
		- Plots for actuator values are out of the scope at this moment, but during the design phase consider that this might be a future requirement
